Poker-Eval

VERSION 0.10

Deal, score, and evaluate poker hands for many variants via a named
Poker::Game API (Hold'em, Omaha, draw, stud, Badugi, and more).

SYNOPSIS

    use Poker::Game::Holdem;

    my $game = Poker::Game::Holdem->new;
    my $hero = $game->deal_hole(['As', 'Kd']);
    $game->flop(['Ah', '7c', '2d']);
    $game->turn('9s');
    $game->river('3c');
    $game->evaluate($hero);
    print $hero->name, "\n";

NAMED GAMES (primary API)

    Community:  Holdem, HoldemJokersWild, Pineapple, CrazyPineapple,
                Omaha, OmahaHiLo, Omaha5, Omaha5HiLo,
                Courcheval, CourchevalHiLo
    Draw:       FiveCardDraw, FiveCardDrawDeucesWild,
                FiveCardDrawJokersWild,
                Low27SingleDraw, Low27TripleDraw,
                LowA5SingleDraw, LowA5TripleDraw
    Stud:       SevenCardStud, SevenCardStudHiLo, Razz
    Badugi:     Badugi, Badacey, Badeucy

Advanced users can still compose Poker::Eval::* rules with
Poker::Score::* ranking systems directly.

Only Poker::Eval defines $VERSION for the distribution (cleaner CPAN index).

INSTALLATION

    perl Makefile.PL
    make
    make test
    make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

    perldoc Poker::Eval
    perldoc Poker::Game::Holdem

